Engineering-only companion fix 2 (not a scientific change):

Matched-mechanism requirement 2 says the inactive global clipping threshold must be VERIFIED
from logged gradient norms. Upstream sends `grad_norm` only to wandb, which the matched run
disables. This mirrors it into the console log so both arms leave an auditable record.

