Capacity-restored G1 requirement (README §"one further experiment" the user authorized after
the isolated G1 negative): LoRA must be restored identically in both arms but receive
ACTION-loss gradient only, so it gives the action path non-shared capacity while the WAM
adapters remain the sole route from future supervision into the deployed policy. This cannot be
done with a config flag because the video branch's forward pass also runs through LoRA; it
requires routing at backward time.

